## Why This Is Asked
This probes multi-tenant governance, scale, streaming semantics, schema drift handling, and retention policies across a large lakehouse. It also tests trade-offs between Spark and Flink for high-volume streaming and the practicality of per-tenant partitioning and access control.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant data contracts and lineage
- Exactly-once streaming and idempotent upserts
- Iceberg partitioning by tenant/region
- Schema drift handling and canonical schema
- Data retention, GDPR-style deletes, and privacy masking

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: validate event against per-tenant contract before upsert
function process(event, tenant) {
  const contract = registry.get(tenant);
  if (!contract.validate(event)) throw new Error('Contract violation');
  iceberg.merge(event, canonicalKey, tenant);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test contract drift across tenants over time?
- What metrics and alerts would you monitor for data quality and lineage?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design multi-tenant data contracts, runtime validation, privacy masking, and governance in a real-time setting. Also probes trade-offs between Spark and Flink, plus testing strategies and observability.

## Key Concepts

- Runtime data contracts per tenant
- Per-tenant masking/redaction strategies
- GDPR deletion and data sovereignty
- Schema evolution in lakehouse (Iceberg/Parquet)
- Policy engine governance (e.g., OPA)
- Spark Structured Streaming vs Flink trade-offs
- Testing, monitoring, data quality

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo runtime contract check
function validateRecord(record, contract) {
  for (const field of Object.keys(contract.fields)) {
    if (!record.hasOwnProperty(field) && contract.fields[field].required) {
      throw new Error(`Missing required field ${field}`);
    }
  }
  // redaction example
  if (contract.mask) {
    for (const f of contract.mask) {
      if (record[f]) record[f] = "REDACTED";
    }
  }
  return record;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test per-tenant masking guarantees in CI/CD?
- How would GDPR deletion requests propagate through streaming pipelines and downstream consumers?
